Subject: media: i2c: vd55g1: support the Surface Pro 12 (Intel) IR camera

The Surface Pro 12 (Intel) describes its VD55G0 as ACPI SMO55F0
(\_SB.PC00.I2C3.CAM3, 0x60, one lane) powered by an INT3472 (ICL1) that
provides "avdd" and "dovdd" and the reset GPIO.

- Match SMO55F0 and, on ACPI, request the INT3472 supply names.
- Defer probe until ipu-bridge has created the endpoint.
- Use the Surface Pro 12 Windows driver's 19.2 MHz mode table. Unlike the
  Surface Pro 11 table it sets GPIO0/GPIO1 (0x0469/0x046a) to strobe,
  which drives the IR illuminator; the firmware patch is identical.
---
diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/vd55g0-win.h b/drivers/media/i2c/vd55g0-win.h
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/vd55g0-win.h
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/vd55g0-win.h
@@ -1,8 +1,14 @@
